From edbfd8afa33963fdd289e462a935901c46d759f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:47:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] 3D Video Settings window: only the choices that are the
 program's

Enable 3D, the shortcut to the display settings, and for the video playing the packing it is taken for (every packing and the depth layouts) and the swap of left and right eyes. The packing joins the swap in the per-file store (group StereoVideo, next to what the program keeps per file) and is restored when the file is played again; a choice back at its default is unmarked. The resizing filter, the color depth, the shape fallback and the depth drawing choices leave the window: they are the engine's and keep their values.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
